<title>USA: AMBAC qualifies six muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>AMBAC qualifies six muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMBAC Indemnity Corp said Monday it qualified for bond insurance the following six municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Carroll Community School District, Iowa, $2 million school bonds.  </p>
<p>--Johnston, Iowa, $2.07 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Gibraltar School District, Mich., $7.71 million GOs.</p>
<p>--North Muskegon Public School District, Mich., $8.2 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Reeths-Puffer Schools, Mich., $4.9 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Anderson County, Tenn., $17.34 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
